<%- include('../../partials/header') %>
<style>
body{background:#f5f7fa;}
.io-wrap{max-width:1320px;margin:0 auto;padding:2rem 1.5rem 4rem;display:grid;grid-template-columns:220px 1fr 260px;gap:2rem;align-items:start;}
.io-toc{position:sticky;top:6rem;background:#fff;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #e8edf5;box-shadow:0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.04);overflow:hidden;}
.io-toc-head{background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0ea5e9,#0284c7);color:#fff;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;font-size:.85rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.8px;}
.io-toc-list{list-style:none;padding:.75rem 0;margin:0;}
.io-toc-list li a{display:block;padding:.5rem 1.25rem;font-size:.84rem;color:#475569;text-decoration:none;border-left:3px solid transparent;transition:all .18s;line-height:1.4;}
.io-toc-list li a:hover,.io-toc-list li a.io-toc-active{color:#0284c7;background:#f0f9ff;border-left-color:#0ea5e9;}
.io-toc-div{height:1px;background:#f1f5f9;margin:.5rem 0;}
.io-toc-rlbl{padding:.5rem 1.25rem;font-size:.78rem;font-weight:700;color:#94a3b8;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px;}
.io-toc-rlist{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 .75rem;}
.io-toc-rlist li a{display:block;padding:.4rem 1.25rem;font-size:.82rem;color:#64748b;text-decoration:none;transition:color .15s;}
.io-toc-rlist li a:hover{color:#0284c7;}
.io-main{min-width:0;}
.io-hero{margin-bottom:2rem;}
.io-hero h1{font-size:2.1rem;color:#0f172a;margin:0 0 .6rem;line-height:1.25;}
.io-desc{font-size:1.05rem;color:#64748b;line-height:1.65;margin:0 0 .75rem;border-left:4px solid #7dd3fc;padding-left:1rem;}
.io-bc{font-size:.8rem;color:#94a3b8;margin-bottom:.75rem;}
.io-bc a{color:#64748b;text-decoration:none;}
.io-bc a:hover{color:#0284c7;}
/* Card */
.io-card{background:#fff;border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.05);border:1px solid #eef2f7;margin-bottom:2.5rem;overflow:hidden;}
.io-tabs{display:flex;border-bottom:1px solid #e2e8f0;background:#f8fafc;}
.io-tab{flex:1;text-align:center;padding:1rem .5rem;font-size:.88rem;font-weight:600;color:#64748b;cursor:pointer;border-bottom:3px solid transparent;transition:all .2s;background:none;border-top:none;border-left:none;border-right:none;}
.io-tab:hover{color:#0284c7;background:#f0f9ff;}
.io-tab.active{color:#0284c7;border-bottom-color:#0ea5e9;background:#fff;}
.io-inner{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;}
.io-form-col{padding:2rem;border-right:1px solid #f0f4fa;}
.io-res-col{padding:2rem;background:linear-gradient(160deg,#f8fafc,#f0f9ff);}
.io-panel{display:none;}
.io-panel.active{display:block;}
.io-panel-desc{font-size:.85rem;color:#64748b;margin-bottom:1.5rem;line-height:1.5;}
.io-field{margin-bottom:1.2rem;}
.io-field label{display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:.9rem;color:#1e293b;margin-bottom:.4rem;}
.io-field input,.io-field select{width:100%;padding:12px 15px;border:1.5px solid #d1dae8;border-radius:8px;font-size:1rem;color:#0f172a;outline:none;transition:border-color .2s,box-shadow .2s;box-sizing:border-box;background:#fff;}
.io-field input:focus,.io-field select:focus{border-color:#0ea5e9;box-shadow:0 0 0 3px rgba(14,165,233,.12);}
.io-field .io-hint{font-size:.76rem;color:#94a3b8;margin-top:.3rem;line-height:1.4;}
.io-row2{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem;}
.io-btn{width:100%;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0ea5e9,#0284c7);color:#fff;padding:15px;border:none;border-radius:9px;font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;margin-top:.75rem;transition:opacity .2s,transform .15s;}
.io-btn:hover{opacity:.92;transform:translateY(-1px);}
/* Results */
.io-res-head{font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:700;color:#0f172a;margin:0 0 .25rem;}
.io-res-sub{font-size:.84rem;color:#64748b;margin:0 0 1.25rem;}
.io-primary{background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0ea5e9,#0284c7);border-radius:10px;padding:1.35rem 1rem;text-align:center;box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(14,165,233,.25);margin-bottom:.75rem;}
.io-primary-val{display:block;font-size:2.4rem;font-weight:800;color:#fff;line-height:1;margin-bottom:.2rem;}
.io-primary-lbl{font-size:.88rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,.8);}
.io-boxes{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.7rem;margin-bottom:.85rem;}
.io-box{background:#fff;border:1.5px solid #e8edf5;border-radius:10px;padding:.85rem .75rem;text-align:center;}
.io-box-val{display:block;font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:800;color:#0284c7;margin-bottom:.15rem;}
.io-box-lbl{font-size:.72rem;color:#64748b;font-weight:600;line-height:1.3;}
/* Phase comparison */
.io-phase{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;padding:.9rem 1rem;margin-bottom:.75rem;}
.io-phase-title{font-size:.72rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;color:#94a3b8;margin-bottom:.6rem;}
.io-phase-row{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;padding:.3rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #f8fafc;font-size:.85rem;}
.io-phase-row:last-child{border-bottom:none;}
.io-phase-lbl{color:#64748b;}
.io-phase-val{font-weight:700;color:#1e293b;}
.io-phase-shock{background:#fff7ed;border:1.5px solid #fed7aa;border-radius:8px;padding:.6rem .75rem;margin-top:.5rem;font-size:.82rem;color:#9a3412;line-height:1.5;}
/* Bar */
.io-bar-wrap{margin-bottom:.75rem;}
.io-bar-label{font-size:.72rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;color:#94a3b8;margin-bottom:.35rem;}
.io-bar-track{display:flex;height:1.6rem;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;}
.io-bar-io{background:#0ea5e9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;color:#fff;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;transition:width .4s;}
.io-bar-pi{background:#6366f1;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;color:#fff;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;transition:width .4s;}
.io-bar-int{background:#f59e0b;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;color:#fff;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;transition:width .4s;}
.io-bar-legend{display:flex;gap:.75rem;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:.72rem;color:#64748b;margin-top:.3rem;}
.io-dot{display:inline-block;width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:2px;margin-right:.2rem;vertical-align:middle;}
/* Amortization */
.io-amort-toggle{width:100%;text-align:left;background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:.75rem 1rem;font-size:.85rem;font-weight:600;color:#475569;cursor:pointer;margin-top:.5rem;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;}
.io-amort-toggle:hover{background:#f0f9ff;color:#0284c7;}
.io-amort-wrap{display:none;margin-top:.5rem;overflow-x:auto;}
.io-amort-wrap.show{display:block;}
.io-amort-table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.78rem;}
.io-amort-table th{background:#0284c7;color:#fff;padding:8px 10px;text-align:right;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap;}
.io-amort-table th:first-child{text-align:left;}
.io-amort-table td{padding:6px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid #f1f5f9;text-align:right;color:#334155;}
.io-amort-table td:first-child{text-align:left;color:#0f172a;font-weight:600;}
.io-amort-table tr.io-phase-switch{background:#fef9c3;}
.io-amort-table tr.io-phase-switch td{color:#92400e;font-weight:700;}
.io-amort-table tr:hover td{background:#f0f9ff;}
/* Content sections */
.io-section{background:#fff;border-radius:14px;border:1px solid #eef2f7;box-shadow:0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.03);padding:2.25rem;margin-bottom:2rem;scroll-margin-top:6rem;}
.io-section h2{font-size:1.65rem;color:#0f172a;margin:0 0 1.25rem;padding-bottom:.75rem;border-bottom:2px solid #f0f4fa;}
.io-section h3{font-size:1.18rem;color:#1e293b;margin:1.75rem 0 .7rem;}
.io-section p{color:#475569;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.25rem;}
.io-section ul,.io-section ol{color:#475569;line-height:1.75;padding-left:1.5rem;margin-bottom:1.25rem;}
.io-section li{margin-bottom:.5rem;}
.io-section strong{color:#1e293b;}
.io-section a{color:#0284c7;}
.io-formula{background:#0f172a;color:#7dd3fc;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:1rem;padding:1.1rem 1.4rem;border-radius:8px;margin:1.25rem 0;line-height:1.9;}
.io-formula code{display:block;}
.io-table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid #e8edf5;margin-bottom:1.5rem;}
.io-table th{background:#0284c7;color:#fff;padding:13px 16px;text-align:left;font-size:.88rem;font-weight:600;}
.io-table td{padding:11px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid #f1f5f9;font-size:.9rem;color:#334155;}
.io-table tr:last-child td{border-bottom:none;}
.io-table tr:nth-child(even) td{background:#f8fafc;}
.io-info{background:#f0f9ff;border-left:4px solid #0ea5e9;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:1.25rem 0;font-size:.95rem;color:#075985;line-height:1.6;}
.io-warn{background:#fff7ed;border-left:4px solid #f97316;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:1.25rem 0;font-size:.95rem;color:#9a3412;line-height:1.6;}
.io-faq-item{border-bottom:1px solid #f0f4fa;padding-bottom:1.25rem;margin-bottom:1.25rem;}
.io-faq-item:last-child{border-bottom:none;margin-bottom:0;padding-bottom:0;}
.io-faq-q{font-size:1.02rem;font-weight:700;color:#0f172a;margin-bottom:.6rem;cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-start;gap:1rem;}
.io-faq-q::after{content:'+';font-size:1.3rem;color:#0ea5e9;flex-shrink:0;}
.io-faq-item.open .io-faq-q::after{content:'−';}
.io-faq-a{color:#475569;line-height:1.7;font-size:.97rem;display:none;}
.io-faq-item.open .io-faq-a{display:block;}
/* Sidebar */
.io-sidebar{position:sticky;top:6rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1.25rem;}
.io-widget{background:#fff;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #e8edf5;box-shadow:0 4px 18px rgba(0,0,0,.05);overflow:hidden;}
.io-widget-head{background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0ea5e9,#0284c7);color:#fff;padding:1rem 1.25rem;}
.io-widget-title{font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;}
.io-widget-sub{font-size:.8rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,.75);}
.io-widget-upd{font-size:.72rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,.6);margin-top:.35rem;}
.io-widget-rows{padding:.4rem 0;}
.io-widget-row{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;padding:.6rem 1.25rem;border-bottom:1px solid #f8fafc;transition:background .15s;}
.io-widget-row:last-child{border-bottom:none;}
.io-widget-row:hover{background:#f0f9ff;}
.io-wl{font-size:.82rem;font-weight:600;color:#334155;}
.io-ws{font-size:.72rem;color:#94a3b8;}
.io-wv{font-size:.92rem;font-weight:800;color:#0284c7;text-align:right;white-space:nowrap;}
.io-widget-foot{padding:.85rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f0f4fa;background:#f8fafc;}
.io-widget-foot p{font-size:.75rem;color:#64748b;margin:0 0 .5rem;line-height:1.3;}
.io-widget-foot a{font-size:.83rem;font-weight:700;color:#0284c7;text-decoration:none;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.35rem;}
.io-widget-foot a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}
.io-quick-widget{background:#fff;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #e8edf5;box-shadow:0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.04);overflow:hidden;}
.io-quick-head{padding:.9rem 1.25rem;background:#f8fafc;border-bottom:1px solid #f0f4fa;font-size:.83rem;font-weight:700;color:#475569;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px;}
.io-quick-links{list-style:none;padding:.5rem 0;margin:0;}
.io-quick-links li a{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;padding:.65rem 1.25rem;font-size:.85rem;color:#475569;text-decoration:none;border-left:3px solid transparent;transition:all .15s;font-weight:500;}
.io-quick-links li a:hover,.io-quick-links li a.active{color:#0284c7;background:#f0f9ff;border-left-color:#0ea5e9;}
@media(max-width:1200px){.io-wrap{grid-template-columns:200px 1fr 240px;}}
@media(max-width:1024px){.io-wrap{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.io-toc,.io-sidebar{position:static;}.io-sidebar{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;}}
@media(max-width:768px){.io-wrap{padding:1rem 1rem 3rem;}.io-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.io-form-col{border-right:none;border-bottom:1px solid #f0f4fa;}.io-sidebar{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.io-row2{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.io-tabs{flex-wrap:wrap;}.io-tab{font-size:.8rem;padding:.75rem .35rem;}.io-boxes{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;}}
</style>

<main id="main-content">
<div class="io-wrap">

  <!-- LEFT TOC -->
  <aside class="io-toc">
    <div class="io-toc-head">📋 In This Article</div>
    <ul class="io-toc-list">
      <li><a href="#calculator" class="io-toc-active">IO Loan Calculator</a></li>
      <li><a href="#how-it-work">How It Works</a></li>
      <li><a href="#formula">The Formula</a></li>
      <li><a href="#payment-shock">Payment Shock</a></li>
      <li><a href="#heloc">HELOC Guide</a></li>
      <li><a href="#construction">Construction Loans</a></li>
      <li><a href="#pros-con">Pros &amp; Cons</a></li>
      <li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="io-toc-div"></div>
    <div class="io-toc-rlbl">Related Calculators</div>
    <ul class="io-toc-rlist">
      <li><a href="<%= baseUrl %>/loan-calculators/personal-loan-calculator">Personal Loan</a></li>
      <li><a href="<%= baseUrl %>/loan-calculators/business-loan-calculator">Business Loan</a></li>
      <li><a href="<%= baseUrl %>/loan-calculators/land-loan-calculator">Land Loan</a></li>
      <li><a href="<%= baseUrl %>/real-estate/cap-rate-calculator">Cap Rate Calculator</a></li>
    </ul>
  </aside>

  <!-- MAIN -->
  <div class="io-main">
    <div class="io-hero">
      <div class="io-bc">
        <a href="<%= baseUrl %>/index.php">Home</a> ›
        <a href="<%= baseUrl %>/loan-calculators/">Loan Calculators</a> ›
        Interest Only Loan Calculator
      </div>
      <h1>Interest Only Loan Calculator (<%= currentYear %>)</h1>
      <p class="io-desc">
        Calculate <strong>interest-only monthly payments</strong>, see the exact
        <strong>payment shock</strong> when principal kicks in, and get a full
        amortization schedule — for <strong>mortgages</strong>, <strong>HELOCs</strong>,
        and <strong>construction loans</strong>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- CALCULATOR -->
    <div class="io-card" id="calculator">
      <div class="io-tab">
        <button class="io-tab active" data-panel="io-mortgage">🏠 IO Mortgage</button>
        <button class="io-tab"        data-panel="io-heloc">💳 HELOC</button>
        <button class="io-tab"        data-panel="io-construction">🏗️ Construction Loan</button>
      </div>
      <div class="io-inner">

        <!-- FORM -->
        <div class="io-form-col">

          <!-- IO Mortgage -->
          <div id="io-mortgage" class="io-panel active">
            <p class="io-panel-desc">For interest-only purchase mortgages or refinances. Calculates IO period payment, fully-amortized payment after IO ends, and total interest cost.</p>
            <div class="io-row2">
              <div class="io-field">
                <label for="m_amount">Loan Amount ($)</label>
                <input type="number" id="m_amount" value="400000" min="1000" step="1000">
                <div class="io-hint">Purchase price minus down payment</div>
              </div>
              <div class="io-field">
                <label for="m_rate">Annual Interest Rate (%)</label>
                <input type="number" id="m_rate" value="7.0" min="0.1" max="30" step="0.05">
                <div class="io-hint">Current 30-yr IO rates: ~7.0–7.75%</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="io-row2">
              <div class="io-field">
                <label for="m_io_year">Interest-Only Period (yrs)</label>
                <input type="number" id="m_io_year" value="10" min="1" max="20" step="1">
                <div class="io-hint">Typically 5–10 years</div>
              </div>
              <div class="io-field">
                <label for="m_term">Total Loan Term (yrs)</label>
                <input type="number" id="m_term" value="30" min="1" max="40" step="1">
                <div class="io-hint">30 years is most common</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="io-field">
              <label for="m_extra">Extra Monthly Principal Payment ($) <span style="font-weight:400;color:#94a3b8;">(optional)</span></label>
              <input type="number" id="m_extra" value="0" min="0" step="50">
              <div class="io-hint">Paying extra during IO period reduces future payment shock</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- HELOC -->
          <div id="io-heloc" class="io-panel">
            <p class="io-panel-desc">HELOC draw period is typically 10 years interest-only. After draw period, a 20-year repayment phase begins with full principal + interest payments.</p>
            <div class="io-row2">
              <div class="io-field">
                <label for="h_balance">Current Balance Drawn ($)</label>
                <input type="number" id="h_balance" value="75000" min="1000" step="1000">
                <div class="io-hint">Amount currently drawn from credit line</div>
              </div>
              <div class="io-field">
                <label for="h_rate">Current Rate (%)</label>
                <input type="number" id="h_rate" value="9.25" min="0.1" max="30" step="0.05">
                <div class="io-hint">HELOC rates are variable — avg ~9.0–9.5% in <%= currentYear %></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="io-row2">
              <div class="io-field">
                <label for="h_draw_rem">Draw Period Remaining (yrs)</label>
                <input type="number" id="h_draw_rem" value="7" min="0" max="10" step="1">
              </div>
              <div class="io-field">
                <label for="h_repay">Repayment Period (yrs)</label>
                <input type="number" id="h_repay" value="20" min="1" max="30" step="1">
                <div class="io-hint">Typically 20 years after draw period</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Construction Loan -->
          <div id="io-construction" class="io-panel">
            <p class="io-panel-desc">Construction loans are interest-only during the build phase. Funds are drawn progressively — this calculates your average IO payment based on expected total draw.</p>
            <div class="io-row2">
              <div class="io-field">
                <label for="c_total">Total Loan Amount ($)</label>
                <input type="number" id="c_total" value="350000" min="10000" step="5000">
                <div class="io-hint">Total approved construction budget</div>
              </div>
              <div class="io-field">
                <label for="c_rate">Construction Rate (%)</label>
                <input type="number" id="c_rate" value="8.5" min="1" max="20" step="0.05">
                <div class="io-hint">Typically prime + 1–2% for construction</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="io-row2">
              <div class="io-field">
                <label for="c_month">Build Duration (months)</label>
                <input type="number" id="c_month" value="12" min="3" max="36" step="1">
                <div class="io-hint">Typical: 6–18 months for new construction</div>
              </div>
              <div class="io-field">
                <label for="c_perm_rate">Permanent Loan Rate (%)</label>
                <input type="number" id="c_perm_rate" value="7.0" min="1" max="20" step="0.05">
                <div class="io-hint">Rate after conversion to permanent mortgage</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="io-row2">
              <div class="io-field">
                <label for="c_perm_term">Permanent Loan Term (yrs)</label>
                <input type="number" id="c_perm_term" value="30" min="10" max="40" step="1">
              </div>
              <div class="io-field">
                <label for="c_draw_pct">Avg Draw at Midpoint (%)</label>
                <input type="number" id="c_draw_pct" value="50" min="10" max="100" step="5">
                <div class="io-hint">At 50%, avg monthly IO payment uses half total loan</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <button class="io-btn" id="io-calc-btn">⚡ Calculate</button>
        </div>

        <!-- RESULTS -->
        <div class="io-res-col">
          <h3 class="io-res-head">Results</h3>
          <p class="io-res-sub" id="io-res-sub">Adjust inputs and click Calculate</p>

          <div class="io-primary">
            <span class="io-primary-val" id="io-primary-val">$2,333/mo</span>
            <span class="io-primary-lbl" id="io-primary-lbl">Interest-Only Monthly Payment</span>
          </div>

          <div class="io-boxe">
            <div class="io-box"><span class="io-box-val" id="io-box1">$3,101</span><span class="io-box-lbl" id="io-box1-lbl">Full Payment After IO</span></div>
            <div class="io-box"><span class="io-box-val" id="io-box2">$768</span><span class="io-box-lbl" id="io-box2-lbl">Payment Increase</span></div>
            <div class="io-box"><span class="io-box-val" id="io-box3">$624,287</span><span class="io-box-lbl" id="io-box3-lbl">Total Interest Paid</span></div>
            <div class="io-box"><span class="io-box-val" id="io-box4">$1,024,287</span><span class="io-box-lbl" id="io-box4-lbl">Total Amount Paid</span></div>
          </div>

          <!-- Phase comparison -->
          <div class="io-phase">
            <div class="io-phase-title">Phase Comparison</div>
            <div class="io-phase-row"><span class="io-phase-lbl">IO Period</span><span class="io-phase-val" id="ph-io-period">—</span></div>
            <div class="io-phase-row"><span class="io-phase-lbl">IO Monthly Payment</span><span class="io-phase-val" id="ph-io-pay">—</span></div>
            <div class="io-phase-row"><span class="io-phase-lbl">Amortization Period</span><span class="io-phase-val" id="ph-am-period">—</span></div>
            <div class="io-phase-row"><span class="io-phase-lbl">Full Monthly Payment</span><span class="io-phase-val" id="ph-am-pay">—</span></div>
            <div class="io-phase-row"><span class="io-phase-lbl">Interest During IO Phase</span><span class="io-phase-val" id="ph-io-int">—</span></div>
            <div class="io-phase-row"><span class="io-phase-lbl">Interest After IO Phase</span><span class="io-phase-val" id="ph-am-int">—</span></div>
            <div class="io-phase-shock" id="ph-shock">—</div>
          </div>

          <!-- Cost bar -->
          <div class="io-bar-wrap">
            <div class="io-bar-label">Where Your Money Goes (Total)</div>
            <div class="io-bar-track">
              <div class="io-bar-io"  id="bar-io-int" style="width:30%">IO Int</div>
              <div class="io-bar-int" id="bar-am-int" style="width:35%">Amort Int</div>
              <div class="io-bar-pi"  id="bar-princ"  style="width:35%">Principal</div>
            </div>
            <div class="io-bar-legend">
              <span><span class="io-dot" style="background:#0ea5e9;"></span>IO Interest</span>
              <span><span class="io-dot" style="background:#f59e0b;"></span>Post-IO Interest</span>
              <span><span class="io-dot" style="background:#6366f1;"></span>Principal</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Amortization toggle -->
          <button class="io-amort-toggle" id="io-amort-toggle">
            <span>📊 Show Full Amortization Schedule</span>
            <span id="io-amort-arrow">▼</span>
          </button>
          <div class="io-amort-wrap" id="io-amort-wrap">
            <table class="io-amort-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Month</th>
                  <th>Phase</th>
                  <th>Payment</th>
                  <th>Principal</th>
                  <th>Interest</th>
                  <th>Balance</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody id="io-amort-body"></tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p style="font-size:.74rem;color:#64748b;margin-top:.5rem;">*Estimates only. Does not include property taxes, insurance, or PMI. Consult your lender for exact figures.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div><!-- /io-card -->

    <!-- HOW IT WORKS -->
    <section class="io-section" id="how-it-work">
      <h2>How Interest-Only Loans Work</h2>
      <p>An interest-only (IO) loan has two distinct phases. During the <strong>IO period</strong> (typically 5–10 years), your monthly payment covers only the interest — your principal balance does not change at all. After the IO period, you enter the <strong>amortization phase</strong>, where your payment jumps significantly because you must now repay 100% of the original principal over a shorter remaining term.</p>

      <h3>The Two Phases in Plain English</h3>
      <table class="io-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Phase</th><th>Duration</th><th>What You Pay</th><th>Balance Change</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Interest-Only Period</strong></td><td>5–10 years (typical)</td><td>Interest only — no principal</td><td>Stays at 100% of original loan</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Amortization Period</strong></td><td>Remaining term (e.g., 20 yrs on a 30-yr loan)</td><td>Principal + Interest — full payment</td><td>Decreases each month</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="io-warn">
        <strong>The hidden cost of IO loans:</strong> On a 30-year mortgage with a 10-year IO period, you have only <em>20 years</em> left to pay off the full original balance — not 30. This compresses the repayment schedule, resulting in higher monthly payments and more total interest than a standard 30-year amortizing loan.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FORMULA -->
    <section class="io-section" id="formula">
      <h2>Interest-Only Loan Payment Formula</h2>
      <p>The IO payment is straightforward — simpler than a standard amortizing payment because no principal is included:</p>

      <h3>Interest-Only Period Payment</h3>
      <div class="io-formula">
        <code>Monthly IO Payment = Loan Balance × (Annual Rate / 12)</code>
        <code>Example: $400,000 × (7.0% A 12) = $400,000 × 0.005833 = $2,333/month</code>
      </div>

      <h3>Fully-Amortized Payment (After IO Period)</h3>
      <div class="io-formula">
        <code>Monthly Payment = P × [r(1+r)^n] A [(1+r)^n − 1]</code>
        <code>P = remaining balance (= original loan if no extra payments made)</code>
        <code>r = monthly rate = Annual Rate / 12</code>
        <code>n = remaining months (e.g., 240 months if 20 years remain)</code>
        <code>Example: $400K at 7%, 20 yrs remaining → $3,101/month</code>
      </div>

      <h3>Payment Shock Calculation</h3>
      <div class="io-formula">
        <code>Payment Shock ($) = Full Amortized Payment − IO Payment</code>
        <code>Payment Shock (%) = (Full Payment / IO Payment − 1) × 100</code>
        <code>Example: ($3,101 − $2,333) = $768 more (+32.9% increase)</code>
      </div>

      <div class="io-info">
        💡 <strong>Reduce payment shock with extra payments:</strong> If you pay $300 extra toward principal each month during a 10-year IO period, you reduce the balance from $400,000 to $364,000 — lowering the post-IO payment from $3,101 to $2,820/month. Use the Extra Payment field in the calculator above to model this.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PAYMENT SHOCK -->
    <section class="io-section" id="payment-shock">
      <h2>Payment Shock — The Most Important Number</h2>
      <p>Payment shock is the sudden and permanent increase in your monthly mortgage payment when the interest-only period ends. It is the primary risk of IO mortgages and the reason lenders are required by the Ability-to-Repay (ATR) rule to qualify borrowers at the fully-amortized payment — not the lower IO payment.</p>

      <h3>Real Payment Shock Examples (<%= currentYear %>)</h3>
      <table class="io-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Loan Amount</th><th>Rate</th><th>IO Period</th><th>IO Payment</th><th>Post-IO Payment</th><th>Shock</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>$300,000</td><td>7.0%</td><td>10 yr (20 yr left)</td><td>$1,750/mo</td><td>$2,326/mo</td><td><strong>+$576 (+33%)</strong></td></tr>
          <tr><td>$400,000</td><td>7.0%</td><td>10 yr (20 yr left)</td><td>$2,333/mo</td><td>$3,101/mo</td><td><strong>+$768 (+33%)</strong></td></tr>
          <tr><td>$600,000</td><td>7.5%</td><td>10 yr (20 yr left)</td><td>$3,750/mo</td><td>$4,833/mo</td><td><strong>+$1,083 (+29%)</strong></td></tr>
          <tr><td>$800,000</td><td>7.25%</td><td>5 yr (25 yr left)</td> <td>$4,833/mo</td><td>$5,791/mo</td><td><strong>+$958 (+20%)</strong></td></tr>
          <tr><td>$1,000,000</td><td>7.5%</td><td>10 yr (20 yr left)</td><td>$6,250/mo</td><td>$8,056/mo</td><td><strong>+$1,806 (+29%)</strong></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:#64748b;">Assumes no extra principal payments during IO period and rate remains constant throughout.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- HELOC -->
    <section class="io-section" id="heloc">
      <h2>HELOC Interest-Only Calculator — How It Works</h2>
      <p>A Home Equity Line of Credit (HELOC) is a revolving credit line secured by your home equity. Most HELOCs have a <strong>10-year draw period</strong> during which you can borrow up to your credit limit and pay interest only on the amount drawn. After the draw period, the <strong>repayment period</strong> begins — typically 20 years of fully amortizing principal + interest payments.</p>

      <h3>HELOC IO Payment Formula</h3>
      <div class="io-formula">
        <code>Monthly IO Payment = Outstanding Balance × (Current Rate / 12)</code>
        <code>Example: $75,000 drawn at 9.25% → $75,000 × (0.0925 / 12) = $578/month</code>
      </div>

      <h3>HELOC vs. Home Equity Loan</h3>
      <table class="io-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>HELOC</th><th>Home Equity Loan</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Rate type</td><td>Variable (Prime + margin)</td><td>Fixed</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Draw structure</td><td>Revolving line — draw as needed</td><td>Lump sum at closing</td></tr>
          <tr><td>IO period</td><td>Yes — typically 10 years</td><td>No — amortizes immediately</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Payment stability</td><td>Varies with rate and balance</td><td>Fixed and predictable</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Ongoing expenses — renovations, tuition</td><td>One-time large expense</td></tr>
          <tr><td><%= currentYear %> typical rate</td><td>Prime + 0.5–1% (~9.0–9.5%)</td><td>8.5–9.5% fixed</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="io-warn">
        <strong>HELOC rate risk:</strong> HELOCs are variable-rate products. The Federal Reserve's rate cycle directly impacts your HELOC payment. A 1% rate increase on a $100,000 HELOC balance adds $83/month to your IO payment. Always model worst-case scenarios (rate + 2%) when qualifying for a HELOC.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CONSTRUCTION -->
    <section class="io-section" id="construction">
      <h2>Construction Loan Interest-Only Calculator</h2>
      <p>Construction loans are almost universally interest-only during the <strong>construction phase</strong> (typically 6–24 months). Unlike a standard mortgage, funds are disbursed in stages (called "draw") as construction milestones are completed — so you only pay interest on the amount actually drawn, not the full loan amount.</p>

      <h3>How Construction Loan IO Payments Work</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Month 1–3:</strong> Foundation and framing draws (~25–30% of loan) → small IO payment</li>
        <li><strong>Month 4–8:</strong> Mechanical, electrical, plumbing draws (~50–60% drawn) → growing IO payment</li>
        <li><strong>Month 9–12+:</strong> Finishing draws (~75–100% drawn) → near-maximum IO payment</li>
        <li><strong>At completion:</strong> Loan converts to permanent mortgage (construction-to-perm) or is refinanced</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="io-formula">
        <code>Monthly IO Payment = Amount Drawn × (Rate / 12)</code>
        <code>Avg payment during build = Total Loan × Avg Draw% × (Rate / 12)</code>
        <code>Example: $350,000 loan, 50% avg draw, 8.5% → $350K × 0.50 × 0.007083 = $1,240/mo avg</code>
      </div>

      <div class="io-info">
        💡 <strong>Construction-to-permanent loans</strong> (also called "one-time close") combine the construction and permanent mortgage into one loan, saving you from a second round of closing costs. The loan automatically converts to a standard 30-year mortgage when construction is complete. This calculator's Construction mode shows both the IO build-phase payments and the post-conversion permanent payment.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PROS & CONS -->
    <section class="io-section" id="pros-con">
      <h2>Interest-Only Loan Pros &amp; Cons</h2>
      <h3>Pros</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Lower initial payments.</strong> IO payments are 20–35% lower than fully-amortizing payments, freeing cash flow for other investments or expenses.</li>
        <li><strong>Flexibility for high earners with variable income.</strong> Commission-based earners, business owners, and investors can pay minimums in slow months and make principal lump-sum payments in good months.</li>
        <li><strong>Investment leverage.</strong> If you can earn more than your mortgage rate by investing the payment difference, IO loans can make mathematical sense. At 7% mortgage rate, you'd need investment returns above 7% after tax to justify this strategy.</li>
        <li><strong>Useful for short hold periods.</strong> Investors who plan to sell in 3–5 years never experience payment shock — they capture appreciation without the higher amortizing payment.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Cons</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Zero equity buildup.</strong> You build no equity through payments — only through appreciation. If prices fall, you can go underwater immediately.</li>
        <li><strong>Payment shock is real and significant.</strong> A 30–40% payment increase after the IO period is not hypothetical — it is mathematically guaranteed unless you have paid down significant principal.</li>
        <li><strong>Higher total interest cost.</strong> IO loans cost more in total interest than standard amortizing loans because the principal balance stays higher for longer.</li>
        <li><strong>Qualification is harder.</strong> Lenders must qualify you at the fully-amortized payment (ATR rule), so you must prove you can afford the higher payment even if you're not paying it yet.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="io-section" id="faq">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <div class="io-faq-item open">
        <div class="io-faq-q">How do I calculate an interest-only loan payment?</div>
        <div class="io-faq-a">Multiply your loan balance by the monthly interest rate: <strong>Monthly IO Payment = Balance × (Annual Rate / 12)</strong>. Example: $400,000 at 7.0% → $400,000 × 0.005833 = <strong>$2,333/month</strong>. No principal is included — your balance stays at $400,000 until the IO period ends. Use the calculator above to also see the post-IO payment and total interest cost.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="io-faq-item">
        <div class="io-faq-q">What happens when the interest-only period ends?</div>
        <div class="io-faq-a">Your payment increases — sometimes dramatically. On a 30-year mortgage with a 10-year IO period, you now have 20 years to repay 100% of the original balance. The fully-amortized payment on $400,000 at 7% over the remaining 20 years is $3,101/month — $768 more than the $2,333 IO payment. This 33% increase is called payment shock and is the primary risk of IO loans.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="io-faq-item">
        <div class="io-faq-q">Is an interest-only mortgage a good idea?</div>
        <div class="io-faq-a">It depends on your situation. IO mortgages make sense for: real estate investors with short hold periods, high earners with irregular income, and buyers who will invest the payment difference at returns exceeding the mortgage rate. They are risky for: primary residence buyers who cannot afford the post-IO payment, buyers with no other equity cushion, and anyone in a flat or declining home value market.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="io-faq-item">
        <div class="io-faq-q">What is the current HELOC interest-only payment rate?</div>
        <div class="io-faq-a">In <%= currentYear %>, HELOC rates average 8.75–9.5% (Prime + 0.5–1%). The Prime Rate directly drives HELOC rates. At 9.25%, a $75,000 HELOC balance costs $578/month interest-only. Use the HELOC tab above to calculate your specific payment and see what happens when the 10-year draw period ends and full repayment begins.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="io-faq-item">
        <div class="io-faq-q">How does an interest-only construction loan work?</div>
        <div class="io-faq-a">During construction (typically 6–18 months), you draw funds in stages and pay interest only on the drawn amount. Payments start small and grow as more funds are drawn. At completion, the loan converts to a permanent mortgage (construction-to-perm) or is refinanced. Construction loan rates are typically 1–2% higher than permanent mortgage rates due to lender risk.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="io-faq-item">
        <div class="io-faq-q">Can I make extra payments on an interest-only loan?</div>
        <div class="io-faq-a">Yes — most IO loans allow extra principal payments. Use the Extra Payment field in the calculator above to see the impact. Even $300/month in extra principal payments over a 10-year IO period reduces the balance from $400,000 to $364,000, lowering the post-IO payment by ~$280/month. This is the most effective way to reduce payment shock without refinancing.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="io-faq-item">
        <div class="io-faq-q">Do interest-only loans build equity?</div>
        <div class="io-faq-a">No — IO payments build zero equity. Your balance remains at 100% of the original loan until the amortization phase begins. The only equity you gain during the IO period comes from your initial down payment and home price appreciation. This is why IO loans are risky in flat or declining markets — you have no payment-based equity cushion to absorb value drops.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="io-faq-item">
        <div class="io-faq-q">What is a 40-year interest-only mortgage?</div>
        <div class="io-faq-a">A 40-year IO mortgage typically has a 10-year IO period followed by 30 years of full amortization. Because of the longer amortization period (30 years vs. 20 years on a standard 30-year loan with 10-year IO), the post-IO payment is lower than a standard 30-year mortgage with IO. However, the total interest paid over 40 years is significantly higher. Some lenders offer these as affordability products in high-cost markets.</div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div><!-- /io-main -->

